HST Office: HST PDF windows group under their own taskbar entry (HASONTECH.HSTOffice.Pdf, vn.hasontech.hstoffice-pdf).
Owner decision 14/11/2026. HST PDF is not a module the module manager can identify, so its windows had no
AppUserModelID on Windows (the taskbar grouped them under the executable, apart from every HST icon) and
the default class on Linux.
- framework titlebarupdate: a frame whose controller is the HST PDF viewer (service
  org.hasontech.hstoffice.PdfViewer) gets the application "Pdf": HASONTECH.HSTOffice.Pdf on Windows,
  vn.hasontech.hstoffice-pdf (WM_CLASS / Wayland app id) elsewhere. A PDF tab of an HST Office window
  keeps HST Office's identity.
- scp2: the .pdf ProgID (HSTOffice.Pdf) carries AppUserModelID HASONTECH.HSTOffice.Pdf, so a PDF opened
  from the shell and its jump-list entries match the window; "Open with" and the registered
  capabilities stay HST Draw's (new macro CONDITIONAL_REGISTER_DOC_EXTENSION_APPID).
- sysui pdf.desktop: StartupWMClass=vn.hasontech.hstoffice-pdf, so docks group PDF windows under the
  HST PDF launcher.
License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_pdf_app_user_model_id.py; Windows: tests/runtime/check-windows-document-window-modes.py.
